00:09:39,062 --> 00:09:41,169
to about three percent.

295
00:09:41,417 --> 00:09:43,397
But follow the parts.

296
00:09:43,447 --> 00:09:45,322
In twenty twenty-five,

297
00:09:45,322 --> 00:09:48,040
China's exports to Southeast Asia rose

298
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,727
thirteen percent.

299
00:09:49,947 --> 00:09:52,046
The WTO notes that part of that

300
00:09:52,046 --> 00:09:54,670
growth is parts and materials for products

301
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:57,107
whose buyers live somewhere else.

302
00:09:57,337 --> 00:09:59,362
A new factory can move the final

303
00:09:59,362 --> 00:10:00,151
assembly,

304
00:10:00,151 --> 00:10:01,973
while many of its parts still come

305
00:10:01,973 --> 00:10:03,788
from the old neighborhood.

306
00:10:04,050 --> 00:10:07,150
Moving the deeper layers is slow.

307
00:10:07,230 --> 00:10:09,042
A new plant needs suppliers that don't

308
00:10:09,042 --> 00:10:10,152
exist there yet,

309
00:10:10,152 --> 00:10:11,964
roads and ports that can handle the

310
00:10:11,964 --> 00:10:12,621
volume,

311
00:10:12,621 --> 00:10:13,731
steady power,

312
00:10:13,731 --> 00:10:16,370
and people trained to run the line.

313
00:10:16,490 --> 00:10:18,313
Until all of that arrives,

314
00:10:18,313 --> 00:10:20,347
the boxes keep coming back.

315
00:10:20,583 --> 00:10:21,172
Still,

316
00:10:21,172 --> 00:10:23,323
it is happening.

317
00:10:23,453 --> 00:10:25,367
The IEA says the largest share of

318
00:10:25,367 --> 00:10:28,479
America's electric car imports in twenty

319
00:10:28,479 --> 00:10:30,993
twenty-five came from Mexico.

320
00:10:31,213 --> 00:10:33,785
Battery factory capacity grew faster in

321
00:10:33,785 --> 00:10:35,806
Europe and the United States than in

322
00:10:35,806 --> 00:10:36,773
China.

323
00:10:36,893 --> 00:10:38,493
And in Southeast Asia,

324
00:10:38,493 --> 00:10:41,044
one-third of electric cars sold came from

325
00:10:41,044 --> 00:10:43,268
a Vietnamese carmaker.

326
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,346
The new places face tariffs,

327
00:10:45,346 --> 00:10:46,177
too.

328
00:10:46,207 --> 00:10:48,394
Since July twenty twenty-six,

329
00:10:48,394 --> 00:10:50,852
Vietnam's rate under that same action is

330
00:10:50,852 --> 00:10:52,548
twelve and a half percent,

331
00:10:52,548 --> 00:10:54,377
the same as China's.

332
00:10:54,547 --> 00:10:56,164
Mexico's is ten percent,

333
00:10:56,164 --> 00:10:58,211
with exemptions for goods that follow the

334
00:10:58,211 --> 00:11:00,654
North American trade agreement.

335
00:11:00,917 --> 00:11:02,963
So why does the world still depend

336
00:11:02,963 --> 00:11:04,917
on Chinese factories?

337
00:11:04,917 --> 00:11:07,387
Not because of one cheap wage.

338
00:11:07,387 --> 00:11:08,927
Because of a neighborhood.

339
00:11:08,927 --> 00:11:10,262
Suppliers down the street,

340
00:11:10,262 --> 00:11:12,729
refiners for the hidden materials,

341
00:11:12,729 --> 00:11:14,064
ports that never sleep,

342
00:11:14,064 --> 00:11:16,927
and engineers who have done it before.

343
00:11:17,087 --> 00:11:19,327
Tariffs can move the last step.

344
00:11:19,327 --> 00:11:21,519
Rebuilding the whole neighborhood takes

345
00:11:21,519 --> 00:11:22,677
far longer.

346
00:11:22,677 --> 00:11:23,343
That's why,

347
00:11:23,343 --> 00:11:25,386
even after years of trade war,

348
00:11:25,386 --> 00:11:27,222
more than a quarter of the world's

349
00:11:27,222 --> 00:11:29,518
manufacturing still happens in one

350
00:11:29,518 --> 00:11:30,577
country.

351
00:11:30,647 --> 00:11:32,769
The next factory may well open in

352
00:11:32,769 --> 00:11:33,384
Vietnam,

353
00:11:33,384 --> 00:11:35,177
Mexico or India.

354
00:11:35,177 --> 00:11:37,013
Its parts list is the hard part

355
00:11:37,013 --> 00:11:38,138
to move.

356
00:11:38,383 --> 00:11:39,026
Next time,

357
00:11:39,026 --> 00:11:41,909
we follow the money behind another hidden

358
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:44,283
link of the world economy.

359
00:11:44,413 --> 00:11:46,826
This is The Hidden Economics.
